  "description": "Brass thread insert RX-M2x4 for 3D-printed thermoplastic parts, set by heat (soldering iron) or ultrasound into blind or through holes. M2 internal thread, length 4.0 mm, outer Ø3.6 mm (D1) with opposed spiral knurls, far-end pilot Ø3.1 mm (D2), for a Ø3.2 mm hole (D3) at least 5.0 mm deep (L + 1) with a 1.3 mm minimum wall. Lead-free, cadmium-free brass. Sold 70 per pack (GE-M2x04-001). Used 4 per wearable watch and 6 per smart-bottle cap with M2 x 6 screws.",
  "domains": [
    {
      "dimensions_mm": {
        "height": 4,
        "length": 3.6,
        "width": 3.6
      },
      "domain": "mechanical",
      "material": {
        "assumption": "ruthex names no alloy; 8.5 g/cm³ is within the table's rolled-and-drawn brass range (8.43-8.73) and near 60/40 brass (8.52). The CAD body is the generated nominal shape (19.23 mm³, plain Ø2.0 bore), about 8 % less than the ruthex STEP's 20.95 mm³ with its thread form, so the computed mass (≈ 0.16 g) is about 0.02 g low. Sanity check: ruthex lists a 15 g shipping weight per 70-pack, packaging included, so at most about 0.21 g per insert.",
